# Gate-level regression, on the netlists of `make syn BLOCK=core CORNER=slow` and
# `make syn BLOCK=coproc CORNER=slow` (run both first, with the same technology). Run it with
# `make regress LIST=verif/regress/gls.list`.
# The SDF runs need the slow corner: at typical, the clock-to-Q of a flop that drives another flop
# directly (the stages of a synchronizer, the release of a synchronized reset) is shorter than the
# hold and removal time of the second one. Genus fixes no hold; place and route does, with buffers.
# Before that, the slow delays check the netlist with every flop's own timing checks.
# coproc_cdc_test is left out: it runs clk_acc_i up to 4x faster than clk_i, faster than the
# netlist was synthesized for (ACC_CLK_PERIOD), so with SDF its timing checks fail by design.

TB=tb_rv32_core GLS=1
TB=tb_rv32_core GLS=1 SDF=1

UVM=coproc TEST=coproc_regs_test GLS=1
UVM=coproc TEST=coproc_matmul_directed_test GLS=1
UVM=coproc TEST=coproc_matmul_directed_test GLS=1 SDF=1
UVM=coproc TEST=coproc_matmul_rand_test GLS=1 SDF=1
